00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,380
Chunk-01.

2
00:00:01,380 --> 00:00:05,173
A sharp, tearing sensation ripped through June's lower abdomen.

3
00:00:05,173 --> 00:00:09,238
It was so sudden, so violently intense, that her fingers went numb.

4
00:00:09,238 --> 00:00:11,391
The glass of water slipped from her hand.

5
00:00:11,391 --> 00:00:15,592
It hit the hardwood floor, shattering into dozens of jagged pieces.

6
00:00:15,592 --> 00:00:20,482
The sound echoed loudly in the massive, empty master bedroom of the Compton estate.

7
00:00:20,482 --> 00:00:23,519
June tried to take a step forward, but her knees buckled.

8
00:00:23,519 --> 00:00:28,279
A cold sweat instantly broke out across her forehead, sticking her hair to her skin.

9
00:00:28,279 --> 00:00:32,429
She collapsed onto the expensive Persian rug, her hands flying to her stomach.

10
00:00:32,429 --> 00:00:34,529
Her lungs forgot how to pull in air.

11
00:00:34,529 --> 00:00:39,590
The pain wasn't just a dull ache; it felt like a serrated blade twisting inside her organs.

12
00:00:39,590 --> 00:00:43,280
Her vision blurred at the edges, turning gray.She knew her body.

13
00:00:43,280 --> 00:00:44,986
She was a medical researcher.

14
00:00:44,986 --> 00:00:47,103
This was not a normal pregnancy cramp.

15
00:00:47,103 --> 00:00:48,956
Her vital signs were crashing.

16
00:00:48,956 --> 00:00:51,590
Her phone was on the nightstand, three feet away.

17
00:00:51,590 --> 00:00:52,884
It looked like a mile.

18
00:00:52,884 --> 00:00:56,348
Trembling violently, June dragged her body across the floor.

19
00:00:56,348 --> 00:01:02,472
The jagged pieces of the broken glass bit into her knee, but she couldn't even feel it over the agony in her abdomen.

20
00:01:02,472 --> 00:01:07,476
She reached up, her fingers blindly clawing at the nightstand until she knocked the phone down.

21
00:01:07,476 --> 00:01:09,480
The bright screen pierced her eyes.

22
00:01:09,480 --> 00:01:11,520
Her fingers were slick with cold sweat.

23
00:01:11,520 --> 00:01:14,461
She pressed the speed dial.Number 1. Cole.

24
00:01:14,461 --> 00:01:15,751
The phone rang once.

25
00:01:15,751 --> 00:01:22,713
June squeezed her eyes shut, her fingernails digging so hard into her palms that the skin broke.Please answer.Please.

26
00:01:22,713 --> 00:01:24,150
It rang a second time.

27
00:01:24,150 --> 00:01:28,050
Each second stretched out, heavy and suffocating.Then, a click.

28
00:01:28,050 --> 00:01:30,191
"What. " Cole's voice came through the speaker.

29
00:01:30,191 --> 00:01:31,380
It wasn't a greeting.

30
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:32,892
It was a wall of ice.

31
00:01:32,892 --> 00:01:38,380
In the background, June could hear the clinking of champagne flutes and the smooth jazz of a live band.

32
00:01:38,380 --> 00:01:41,209
"Cole. " June gasped, her throat tight and dry.

33
00:01:41,209 --> 00:01:42,392
"Help me. the baby. "

34
00:01:42,392 --> 00:01:48,020
Before Cole could respond, a high-pitched, sweet voice drifted through the receiver."Cole, who is it.

35
00:01:48,020 --> 00:01:49,872
We're going to be late for the red carpet. "

36
00:01:49,872 --> 00:01:51,939
Alycia.June's stomach lurched.

37
00:01:51,939 --> 00:01:55,165
The pain spiked, sending a wave of nausea up her throat.

38
00:01:55,165 --> 00:01:59,410
"June," Cole said, his tone dropping into a low, impatient growl.

39
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:04,455
"If this is your pathetic attempt to stop me from attending the gala, it's a terrible strategy. "

40
00:02:04,455 --> 00:02:05,789
"No. " June choked out.

41
00:02:05,789 --> 00:02:09,960
She tasted something metallic in her mouth.Blood."I'm bleeding.Please. "

42
00:02:09,960 --> 00:02:11,765
"Stop acting," Cole snapped.

43
00:02:11,765 --> 00:02:16,528
She could almost see him adjusting his expensive cufflinks, annoyed by her existence.

44
00:02:16,528 --> 00:02:17,955
"You are perfectly fine.

45
00:02:17,955 --> 00:02:20,412
We are walking on stage in two minutes.

46
00:02:20,412 --> 00:02:22,657
Do not call this number again tonight. "

47
00:02:22,657 --> 00:02:23,659
"Cole, wait-"

48
00:02:23,659 --> 00:02:27,133
The line went dead.The dial tone buzzed in the silent room.

49
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:28,893
It sounded like a death sentence.

50
00:02:28,893 --> 00:02:31,099
June stared at the darkened screen.

51
00:02:31,099 --> 00:02:34,114
Her phone slipped from her weak grasp, landing on the rug.

52
00:02:34,114 --> 00:02:38,394
A sudden, terrifying warmth spread between her thighs.June looked down.

53
00:02:38,394 --> 00:02:44,108
A dark, thick pool of red was soaking into the intricate patterns of the Persian rug.Blood.So much blood.

54
00:02:44,108 --> 00:02:46,087
A primal panic seized her chest.

55
00:02:46,087 --> 00:02:47,756
She was losing the ba by.

56
00:02:47,756 --> 00:02:53,726
With the last ounce of strength in her shaking fingers, she grabbed the phone again and dialed 911.

57
00:02:53,726 --> 00:02:55,929
"911, what is your emergency. "

58
00:02:55,929 --> 00:03:01,553
"Compton Manor. " June whispered, her voice barely leaving her throat."Hemorrhaging.Pregnant.Please hurry. "

59
00:03:01,553 --> 00:03:02,767
She dropped the phone.

60
00:03:02,767 --> 00:03:04,766
Her head fell back against the floor.

61
00:03:04,766 --> 00:03:10,501
Across the room, the massive flat-screen TV was muted, playing a live broadcast of the charity gala.

62
00:03:10,501 --> 00:03:13,237
Through her half-closed eyes, June saw Cole.

63
00:03:13,237 --> 00:03:16,698
He looked breathtaking in his custom tuxedo.He was smiling.

64
00:03:16,698 --> 00:03:21,044
He was smiling down at Alycia, who had her arm wrapped tightly around his.

65
00:03:21,044 --> 00:03:24,475
Alycia wore a stunning white gown, looking like a bride.

66
00:03:24,475 --> 00:03:29,063
Cole's eyes held a tenderness that June had not seen in four years of marriage.

67
00:03:29,063 --> 00:03:30,586
The contrast was brutal.

68
00:03:30,586 --> 00:03:35,668
He was in the spotlight, holding another woman, while his wife was bleeding out on his bedroom floor.

69
00:03:35,668 --> 00:03:39,826
The wail of ambulance sirens pierced the night air, growing louder.

70
00:03:39,826 --> 00:03:42,715
Downstairs, the heavy oak doors banged open.

71
00:03:42,715 --> 00:03:45,083
Footsteps rushed up the stairs.Mrs.
